# JARVIS (portfolio sessions)

Cross-project knowledge lives at `D:\JARVIS\`. Full contract: skill `jarvis-bridge`
(auto-discovered from `~/.agents/skills/`). Read via `D:\JARVIS\wiki\index.md`; `status:
draft` on a page is curation, not quality — follow draft pages normally.

<!-- JARVIS-DUTY:v1 -->
When this session has actually RUN something worth keeping — a UAT pass, a suite that went
green and was audited, a bug class that earned a name, a perf number measured, a decision
that turned out wrong — write it BEFORE the session ends:
`D:\JARVIS\raw\YYYY-MM-DD-retro-<slug>.md` — first person: what happened, what it cost,
what you would do differently. New file only. Write the note and LEAVE — committing,
logging and distillation belong to the next JARVIS session. If nothing was really run,
do not manufacture a retro.
<!-- /JARVIS-DUTY -->

Portfolio-typical triggers: `pnpm ci-check`, typecheck/lint/build/check-links with a
lesson. Portfolio-specific truth stays in this repo's `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/plans/` —
never copied into the wiki.
